Focus on getting quality sleep , following a sound nutrition plan , doing cardio such as Zone 2 level exercise, and taking supplements . Recommended: 3 Active Recovery Workouts for Your Next Rest Day You could also throw in things like massages, percussive gunwork, stretching, and yoga. Recovery is just as important as the training if you want to get in the best shape possible, so don’t neglect it. Tomorrow’s workout can be better than expected because of what you do today.', PopularityRank=NULL, PopularityWindow=NULL,
        DaysPerWeek=3, ProgramDurationWeeks=10, MinSessionMinutes=60, MaxSessionMinutes=60, EquipmentRequired=N'Barbell, Cables, Dumbbells, Machines', TargetGender=N'Male & Female', WorkoutTypeLabel=N'Split', SourceCategoriesJson=N'["Muscle Building","Men","Strength","Beginner"]', CatalogRank=15
