    SuggestedMonth=NULL, IsSystemDefault=1, SortOrder=10162, SourceUrl=N'https://www.muscleandstrength.com/recipes/chicken-protein-waffles', ImageUrl=N'https://cdn.muscleandstrength.com/sites/default/files/field/feature-image/recipe/protein-chicken-waffles-feature.jpg', ServingSuggestion=N'Makes 2 Servings', ContentText=N'Add chicken breast, milk and hot sauce to a Ziploc bag Shake well and place in the refrigerator overnight The next day, add your special k cereal to a food processor and blend into small pieces (conversely, you can add to a Ziploc back and crush by hand) Put the cereal, cornmeal, paprika, salt and pepper in a Ziploc bag Preheat oven to 400 degrees Line a baking sheet with parchment paper Remove chicken, one piece at a time, from the marinating bag and add to cereal mixture Shake until coated Repeat with all chicken Place coated chicken on baking sheet Bake for 20 minutes Reduce heat to 350 degrees and bake for an additional 15 minutes or until crispy While chicken is cooking, make waffles according to directions Serve chicken on top of waffles Add syrup and butter for a more authentic experience, if desired Notes: *You increase the protein content more by swapping the water for liquid eggwhites when making your waffles and/or increasing the amount of chicken used in the recipe', CategoriesJson=N'["High Protein Recipes","Breakfast Recipes"]', SourceMacrosJson=N'{"calories_kcal":"565","protein_g":"65","carbs_g":"56","fat_g":"9"}', ReadCount=13500
